# Hmisc, VGAM and boot keep package code in `R/*.q` and `R/*.s`, which R CMD INSTALL sources like
# `R/*.R`. The NAMESPACE exports resolve against them, and a `.s` file outside the package's `R/`
# (the one beside DESCRIPTION) is not R.

file DESCRIPTION
| Package: resample
| Version: 0.1.0
file NAMESPACE
| export(boot)
| export(jack)
file R/boot.q
| boot <- function(x) x
file R/jack.s
| jack <- function(x) x
file src/fast.s
| .text
file src/R/vendored.s
| this is ( not R

run ry check
expect exit 0
expect stdout "2 files checked, no problems"
